1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
James Franco is best known to many as a Hollywood actor, but behind the scenes,

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
he's also been a writer, director, college professor, visual artist, and even a doctoral student.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
After rising to fame with roles in Spider-Man and 127 hours, for which he received an Oscar

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
nomination, Franco didn't rest on his success. Instead, he dove headfirst into academia,

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
enrolling at multiple universities. He earned an undergraduate degree from UCLA and MFA in

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
writing from Columbia and went on to pursue a PhD in English at Yale. At one point, Franco taught

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
film and writing at NYU, USC, and UCLA, all while continuing his acting and directing career.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
He also published books, exhibited artwork, and directed films based on classic literature,

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
such as As I Lay Dying in the Sound and the Fury. Though controversial at times,

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
his ability to shift between disciplines has been remarkable. Franco once said,

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
I thrive when I'm busy, I like a challenge. His story is proof that with enough curiosity,

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:21,000
discipline, and drive, one person really can explore multiple passions professionally.

